In promises there's a minor mistake, the asyncHandler you defined just executes instead of returning the wrapped requestHandler, either removing the curly braces or adding a explicit return statenment is needed. Here's the correct code:

const asyncHandler = (requestHandler) => (req, res, next) => {
   Promise.resolve(requestHandler(req, res, next)).catch((err) => next(err));
};

OR

const asyncHandler = (requestHandler) => {
  return (req, res, next) => {
     Promise.resolve(requestHandler(req, res, next)).catch((err) => next(err));
  }
}

