componentWillReceiveProps() is now deprecated.

After struggling for a while trying to replace it with static getDerivedStateFromProps(props, state) [recommended replacement for componentWillReceiveProps()] I was having difficulty trying to map the props to the React state as recommended by the React Documentation. That did not work out well, as mapping props coming from Redux state to the React state was creating errors. I then tried to create a new Redux action to handle updating posts, which was a simple function receiving the current this.props.posts and this.props.newPost and then creating a new array with the new post and dispatching the FETCH_POSTS reducer to update the posts state. In this approach, I was using componentDidUpdate to call this new action creator but I soon (not soon enough) realized that the componentDidUpdate was being called once the NEW_POST action was dispatched and although it did update the posts state with the new post, the React view did not rerender to show the new post even though I had managed to update the Redux posts state with the new post.

So finally if anyone wants to update the posts state directly in Redux instead of updating the list of posts through props:

modify the createPost action to receive the posts state using getStore() and then have the NEW_POST reducer update the 'items' parameter as well instead of just updating 'item', by doing so you also have no need to have the newPost Redux state or the accompanying 'item' parameter as we aren't using React at all to update the list of posts with the newPost.

__postActions.js__
.
.
.
export const createPost = (post) => (dispatch, getStore) => {

  fetch(' {

    method: 'POST',


    headers: {
      'content-type': 'application/json',
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(post),
  })
    .then((res) => res.json())
    .then((post) => {
      let updatedPosts = getStore().posts.items;
      updatedPosts.unshift({ ...post, id: updatedPosts.length + 1 });
      dispatch({
        type: NEW_POST,
        payload: post,
        updatedPosts: updatedPosts,
      });
    });
};

__postReducer.js__
.
.
.
export default function (state = initialState, action) {


  switch (action.type) {
    case FETCH_POSTS:
      return {
        ...state,
        items: action.payload,
      };
    case NEW_POST:
      return {
        ...state,
        item: action.payload,
        items: action.updatedPosts,
      };
    default:
      return state;
  }
}

